<!-- Buying guide (unique local copy; facts from this page, manufacturer spec pages, and /guides/) -->
<section class="pt-70 pb-30">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-lg-9 guide-body">
        <h2>Who Island Spas are for</h2>
        <p>Island Spas suit buyers who want a premium Artesian spa but would rather choose the feature level than pay for everything. You start with the size and seat layout that fits your yard, from mid-size models up to the 9-seat Bimini, then pick a trim. <strong>Essential</strong> covers the fundamentals (32–44 Helix jets, two jet pumps plus a circulation pump, full foam). <strong>Luxury</strong> adds more jets, an enhanced third pump, footblasters and an ozonator. <strong>Elite</strong> goes up to 72 Helix jets and adds DirectFlow personal control and an extended warranty, with a fourth jet pump on the Grand Bahama and Grand Cayman.</p>
        <p>That makes Island Spas a good fit for families who want a full-size spa they'll use every week, and for anyone who wants to put the budget toward hydrotherapy instead of extras they won't use.</p>
        <h2>Electrical and installation</h2>
        <p>Island Spas are full-size 240V spas. The Grand Bahama, for example, uses a 5.5 kW heater, which needs a dedicated circuit installed by a licensed electrician. They're also substantial: the 6-seat Grand Bahama holds about 405 gallons and the 9-seat Bimini about 683 gallons, so plan a level concrete pad or an engineered deck. Our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-cost-utah/">Utah hot tub cost guide</a> breaks down typical installation costs, and <a href="/guides/110v-vs-240v-hot-tubs/">110V vs 240V</a> explains why heater size matters.</p>
        <h2>Island Spas in a Utah winter</h2>
        <p>Every Island Spa trim lists <strong>full-foam insulation</strong>, which is what you want for long soaks in January. Pair it with a tight-fitting <a href="/covers/">cover</a> or a <a href="/covana/">Covana</a> automated cover, and the 5.5 kW heater recovers quickly after the lid has been open. See our <a href="/guides/hot-tub-utah-winter/">winter guide</a> for cold-weather care.</p>
        <h2>See Island Spas in Midvale</h2>
        <p>We keep display models from every brand we carry at 6905 S State St in Midvale (Mon–Sat, 10 AM–5 PM). Floor models change, so <a href="/contact/">call or message us</a> if you want to sit in a specific model before you visit. Bring your yard measurements and we'll help you choose a size and trim.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

